  "id": "method-of-agreement",
  "term": "method of agreement",
  "definition": "The method of agreement is a historical reasoning method that compares several cases in which a phenomenon occurs and looks for the one shared circumstance among otherwise differing cases. That common factor is then taken as evidence of a real connection, usually as a possible cause or effect, though the method is recognized as imperfect and often hard to apply in complex experience.",
